  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Marek and colleagues describe PPMI as an observational, international study designed to establish biomarker-defined cohorts and identify Parkinson’s disease progression markers. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6292383/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c38f689b8fa5b38ba375dcc2c8dcb2850325d3a08e2a059e119916f3d43bcba9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4993525d5079dcf307b3525b237878a2e58710f9938b145a3308ea34076dfa00",
            "ev:76f58f3c6d8b794c0cbfcd83e76786c92174540cbd8f38e469c6da903ec13c52"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NINDS describes the PDBP Data Management Resource as containing clinical, genetic, imaging and biomarker data associated with Parkinson’s disease, Lewy Body Dementia and related disorders. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://pdbp.ninds.nih.gov/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a8cdcf3b20d4a4e7925bec3ff4d70a56a87d74d182e5e8c096cd540ac7e841af",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:74da8cdd29673a97362ee54b82698703bbaa4e72ef03333f936f7ebf00dde2ce"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Iwaki and colleagues describe the AMP Parkinson’s Disease research platform as integrating whole-genome sequencing, RNA expression and clinical data harmonized across cohort studies; NINDS describes the Knowledge Platform as enabling sharing of validated and standardized datasets. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8453903/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:90316e5a048b7ee037e80e3ecc6e414f01343a636e241bbc4886a2979ac3b6c2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:10d4c7def09dd82e1c0e4d1505cc667f95bb6eaaa25ad9e2cce7dce33125e79c",
            "ev:85b928b9000aa748d16e6b6e15627691aa44e3669f0577f91b89f00fb73fe73f",
            "ev:c297d1a41eb5c25b9d21b4d09054c7e927747f2a770025c21094c6602b3cd02c"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/current-research/focus-disorders/parkinsons-disease-research/amp-parkinsons-disease-and-related-disorders"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Parkinson’s Foundation describes PD GENEration as an international research study providing genetic testing and genetic counseling at no cost for people diagnosed with Parkinson’s disease. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/advancing-research/our-research/pdgeneration",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b5c6343bfe5611abcf090cacad481d53ee5ad4da17b2768c1eceb1c24dc54919",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:139ecf25139d5f3ea1fc13070955a3a9023c9c18d58f651ebfc875b5307b371d"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For Parkinson’s disease trials of potential disease-modifying drugs reporting race or ethnicity, Rodrigues and colleagues’ systematic review reports pooled White enrollment of 98%; only 19 of 37 included double-blind randomized placebo-controlled studies reported race or ethnicity. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-12-30)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12834084/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0ab4e5234686de92bd49ce35e60cca0500c450a3ca99313d863e6a76b2348737",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:51f2cb562556306309536af153a6758a5236d500816c117d6c812d8fc9bc6580",
            "ev:cc0be8d4cfe5b18a1decd57974410995f7b36afee63b622d356f1f4ebef05603"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In a UK qualitative study of ethnic minority individuals with Parkinson’s disease, Ramadhan and colleagues identify fatigue, travel difficulties, financial constraints and language barriers among practical barriers to research participation. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-10-24)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12551381/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4d2f510d3775dc365d145a1ea304afec41513952c3f943fd2cde2a928e8adf97",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:617ad776feb2e41094b595dd9720088e1617305f86b7bbcfad2659121676a918",
            "ev:b5e3c00ff9b416eb8cb3a783bc905fa31d78d5b38937a9d35f6c02fef245eeaa",
            "ev:cf75460cd12e2def9b9216da4a906c7626f18bb15a0278a5fdb8b468983dc4bb",
            "ev:eb934afe6f619b6be5073041f8f266374e9b4df6de138516a39dd9ef92f6836f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Parkinson’s Foundation states that the Parkinson’s Outcomes Project, started in 2009, was one of the largest-ever clinical studies of Parkinson’s disease, with more than 13,000 participants in five countries. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/advancing-research/our-research/parkinsons-outcomes-project",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:25b77cde2ae653b8c94ce2ab6acec2ef6742944e7a62a043d635fb79c396df33",
