    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The PPMI participant page states that academic and industry investigators can access the repository after administrative review and completion of a Data Use Agreement requiring privacy protection. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.ppmi-info.org/participants",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:73a58a88bf68d1f2e348a7b85136545f16578031a9a38f2f707aa0060ad09579",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a2f2951e03b7461b24c3b7b6bb27e3f77ed2af65ae0bc4886826e5339271a9bc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The PPMI participant page describes online participation, mailed screening tests and in-person enrollment as distinct participation routes. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.ppmi-info.org/participants",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:420784e6c4196e6bdd3be25e7f9fb5390136a4fb5036f14a2048ef0d03dd0677",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:419fb8178b8a3e5578180767122a0b51fdf47f360f63956a1cd4ab4cce7e0a0c"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Michael J. Fox Foundation describes free at-home PPMI screening for genetic factors and smell ability for people diagnosed with Parkinson’s. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.michaeljfox.org/connect-ppmi-team",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:65fe610e276fe80b049008497cc12ea2ead3752b4db62f5b67d5031b6959e638",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:db7a536f583b0386108c55b943bceafd3a4901f5fd558befcb80abf32c9ae386"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Michael J. Fox Foundation describes Fox Trial Finder as a tool connecting volunteers with recruiting studies through searches based on location and health history, without requiring a login. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.michaeljfox.org/trial-finder",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b51bb5a1b1aea706bcdae6d3c55ac0c9356d9b90eb1adfed41f149ea8a7dab90",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e416c396d2f3fdcb5cbe181b751885462c8d96ef30866fe88a6cde9624549fa1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fox Insight describes collecting self-reported health-experience data online from people with and without Parkinson’s. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://foxinsight.michaeljfox.org/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6e86744a7697db4784ca72ee822f98ac0fa60979f2c4517f2deb0b1bd8513b52",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:198227951b6a5a7b22e1f5a8821870c448bc4882bb48a7b27e5b6953b31f7001",
            "ev:1cb7e8f765017955a13a0c9bc06714137704b2a5c12c086370f6bff2a7eb845a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Parkinson’s Foundation states that studies it lists but does not conduct are provided for convenience and do not constitute endorsement or a recommendation to participate. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/advancing-research/join-study",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0431b398120800b8ed5c4124e7afd966b54f52aa1f161d2aadb3fd6fc53ee32f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0977b15a907c53cb33d1d38424c6668ca75c89185f11e36e0dd65108ad972d6b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Adrissi and colleagues’ community-based study of Parkinson’s research participation in predominantly minority Chicago communities reports transportation and financial incentives as facilitators, and longer visits and study duration as barriers. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-05-29)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12121102/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7f19bf0a5323e6c9801f496d71b9bc76e1a038929b8440a160e75a12a53427bc",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:64389b122f30f82c0f7c2c66389f99fe7c53575c20f86b5a8b8122a1a2e70a46",
            "ev:c0e4d2e26b655275146a715ebb52e4403217e63478d5c5c03aa412d420faec06",
            "ev:e0d5e755e1b9c025024dfc2d0e7e277715ed901c2cd5e342cd865eb668f0cb6f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Parkinson’s Foundation states that the Parkinson’s Outcomes Project has now concluded. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/advancing-research/our-research/parkinsons-outcomes-project",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:584b9c6de9d579b27cda920496959f15e53f070bbfc3fbc00cac0e7c367d0f31",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3465bf904d7526cf8737a17f993d464705ad4c6709436e1c5adfbf35d8cada86"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Parkinson’s Foundation says the Parkinson’s Outcomes Project, with 13,000+ participants, showed that the type and quality of care people receive has a major impact on their symptoms, mobility and long-term health. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/advancing-research/our-research/parkinsons-outcomes-project/findings",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:86188be4cfdf18663697103eb308469a3cb2fe0242464152815b01d0a996939f",
